@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam ParticipantPadding 24
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #42566B
  LifeLineBorderColor #8295A8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #D8EAFE
  ActivationBorderColor #42566B
  ParticipantBorderColor #42566B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F1FA
  ParticipantFontColor #172B4D
  ActorBorderColor #42566B
  ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  GroupBorderColor #8295A8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
  GroupHeaderFontColor #172B4D
  DividerBackgroundColor #E8F1FA
  DividerBorderColor #8295A8
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBEB
  BorderColor #BBA86A
  FontSize 12
}
hide footbox
title UC-T02 - Update Parking Occupancy
actor "External Telemetry System\n(Provider / ACT-03)" as P
boundary "Telemetry API / Adapter" as API
control "TelemetryController" as C
entity "Telemetry & Mobility Records" as D
note over P,D
  What-if events must use isolated run-scoped storage.
end note
P -> API: Submit event (Hub/space, eventRef, observedAt, reporting mode, occupied/free or count)
activate API
API -> C: Process event with source credentials and operational/run scope
activate C
C -> D: Read provider permissions, resource scope and validation policy
activate D
D --> C: Policy / unavailable
deactivate D
C -> C: Verify source identity, resource authorization and operational/run scope
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
alt policy unavailable
C -> C: Set retryable failure; no operational update
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else source or scope unauthorized
C -> D: Record access failure without protected resource details
activate D
D --> C: Audit recorded / audit unavailable
deactivate D
C -> C: Set access denied; never apply event
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else authorized source and scope
C -> C: Validate Hub/space and configured reporting mode, timestamp;\ncount is an integer from 0 to physical capacity
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
alt invalid event / unknown mapping
C -> C: Set validation rejection; retain last accepted state and freshness
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else structurally valid
C -> D: Read original event result/fingerprint and latest accepted observation\nfor this resource/reporting scope (and session when applicable)
activate D
D --> C: Prior result and observation / unavailable
deactivate D
alt event state unavailable
C -> C: Set retryable failure; do not infer availability
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else identical event already processed
C -> C: Use original result; do not advance freshness or repeat effects
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else identity conflict, stale or out-of-order event
C -> D: Retain conflicting evidence where applicable; do not alter accepted observation
activate D
D --> C: Evidence result / unavailable
deactivate D
C -> C: Set rejection reason; do not reset freshness
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else new event satisfies ordering and freshness rules
loop initial attempt; repeat only after concurrency conflict while retry policy permits
C -> D: Read current occupancy records, Active sessions, reservations, unavailable spaces and reporting policy\nand versions in the selected scope
activate D
D --> C: Consistent context / unavailable
deactivate D
alt context unavailable
C -> C: Set retryable failure; stop this retry loop
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else context available
alt aggregate reporting mode
C -> C: Treat count as total observed occupancy, not an increment to Active sessions
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else identified-space reporting mode
C -> C: Reconcile observed space once; do not count an existing occupied space twice
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
end
loop each relevant occupancy record, session and commitment
C -> C: Reconcile without double-counting; preserve reservations and session states
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
end
alt observed and expected occupancy disagree
C -> C: Plan observed/expected discrepancy; withhold disputed capacity from new bookings
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
else observation agrees / no physical change
C -> C: Advance accepted observation time; no repeated occupancy delta;\nresolve prior discrepancy only if reconciliation policy permits
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
end
critical Final event identity, ordering and business-state check + atomic update
C -> D: Atomically commit observation/effects and original processing result only if\nidentity, order, permissions and context versions still match
activate D

D --> C: Committed / original duplicate result / stale or conflicting /\nconcurrency conflict / failed / outcome unknown
deactivate D
end
C -> C: Retry only concurrency conflicts with a fresh context;\notherwise stop loop and classify result
activate C
C --> C: Retry / terminal outcome
deactivate C
end
end
opt outcome unknown
C -> D: Find original processing result using same source, scope and eventRef
activate D
D --> C: Original applied/rejected/failed result / not yet resolved
deactivate D
end
opt newly committed observation/evidence (including recovered commit)
C -> C: Expose accepted time, freshness, restrictions and discrepancies\nfrom committed records to monitoring/detail views
activate C
C --> C: Evaluation result
deactivate C
end
end
end
end
C --> API: Processing result + event reference (applied / original / rejected / retryable / unresolved)
deactivate C
alt acknowledgement delivered
API --> P: Return processing result; unknown is not an applied acknowledgement
else acknowledgement lost
API -> API: Response delivery fails; committed result is retained
activate API
API --> API: Provider may retry same event identity and payload
deactivate API
end
deactivate API
note over P,D
  Observations do not execute Student check-in or checkout.
end note
footer Smart E-Mobility Hub | Submission 2 | External Telemetry
@enduml
